message: "If you use OTShield Bench, please cite the software release."
title: "OTShield Bench"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Jayachandra Reddy"
    family-names: "Palle"
version: "0.6.1-alpha"
date-released: 2026-09-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ASHTHRA/otshield-bench"
url: "https://github.com/ASHTHRA/otshield-bench/releases/tag/v0.6.1-alpha"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22904827"
abstract: >-
  OTShield Bench is a reproducible, vendor-neutral benchmark for operational
  technology cyber-detection effectiveness, resource cost, and resilience under
  degraded connectivity. Version 0.6.1-alpha, dated 2026-09-22, is a research
  release candidate reporting a post-release paired study with 125 completed
  isolated OpenPLC condition runs across five network conditions, 7,500 planned
  transactions, and 250 baseline/robust detector evaluations. The robust threshold
  was fixed using historical clean calibration. Observed resilience differences
  are limited to the documented laboratory and timing setup; they do not establish
  production validation, universal detector superiority, full GRFICS validation,
  DNP3 or EtherNet/IP validation, completed external independent replication, or
  adoption.
keywords:
  - operational technology
  - industrial control systems
  - cybersecurity
  - Modbus TCP
  - OpenPLC
  - detection benchmarking
  - resilience
  - reproducibility
